Install Fail2Ban
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install fail2ban -y

Configure SSH-monitoring
    sudo nano /etc/fail2ban/jail.local

Inside the jail.local
    copy from file in repo
    maxretry = 3 => 3 failed attempts before ban
    batime = 600 => IP is banned for 10 minutes
    findtime = 300 => 3 attemps must occur within 5 minutes

Start og restart fail2ban   
    sudo systemctl restart fail2ban
    sudo systemctl enable fail2ban

Check jail status with fail2ban_status.sh" or this command
    sudo fail2ban-client status sshd

Test Fail2Ban with wrong ssh-login
    ssh wronguser@<target_ip>
    Your IP should be banned after 3 tries

Check banned IP's with script or this command
    sudo fail2ban-client status sshd
    You will see this: 
        Banned IP list: 192.168.1.100

You can remove ban manually
    sudo fail2ban-client sshd unbanip <ip-address>

